# PlayTick Project Context

- The product is **PlayTick**. Never add the former name "Game Progress" to new code, identifiers, strings, or documentation.
- This is a deliberate, reviewable Flutter/Dart portfolio app: favor clear production-quality code over prototypes or enterprise ceremony.
- V1 targets Android and Light Mode. Do not add iOS-specific work or Dark Mode unless explicitly requested.
- Support English and French from the start with Flutter localization. Keep both translations together, use English as fallback, and never hard-code user-facing widget text.
- Keep source identifiers, domain types, and file names in English.
- The core loop is: search IGDB, add to the local library, choose a status, record sessions, derive playtime, then complete or drop the game.
- Main destinations are Home and Library. Game Details is secondary navigation; simple workflows stay in sheets or dialogs.
- Library data is local-first. Existing games, details, notes, and sessions must remain usable when IGDB is unavailable.
- Persist enough IGDB metadata when adding a game to render its local experience offline.
- Valid statuses are `wantToPlay`, `playing`, `completed`, and `dropped`; a new game defaults to `wantToPlay`.
- Prevent duplicate library entries by IGDB ID. A timed session requires `playing`, and only one timed session may be active globally.
- Persist an active session's `startedAt`; derive elapsed time from the current local time rather than storing ticking counters.
- Saved sessions are the sole source of total and weekly playtime. Game notes and session notes are separate concepts.
- Deleting a game must confirm and remove its sessions and notes without orphans.
- Figma is the visual source of truth; written requirements define behavior. Report contradictions instead of guessing.
- Do not add unrequested accounts, cloud/social features, imports, recommendations, advanced dashboards, progress percentages, backend services, or other speculative V1 features.
